@startuml
title Phase IV - Dispatch Waiting-Time NTF Extension Point

package "application.dlv" {
    class DispatchService {
        + dispatch(OrderId) : Optional<Assignment>
        + onCourierIdle() : void
        - requireReadyOrder(Order) : void
        - selectCourier(Order, List<Courier>) : Optional<Courier>
        - isCourierEligible(Courier) : boolean
        - assignCourier(OrderId, Order, Courier) : Assignment
        - findCourier(List<Courier>, UserId) : Courier
        - releaseCancelledCourier(OrderId, Courier) : void
    }

    interface DispatchExtension {
        + onWaitingOrder(OrderId, Instant) : void
        + onAssignmentCreated(OrderId, Assignment) : void
    }
}

package "domain.dlv.delivery" {
    class DispatchQueue
    class Assignment
}

package "domain.dlv.courier" {
    class NearestCourierSelector
    class Courier
}

package "domain.ord.order" {
    class Order
    class OrderId
}

package "NTF module" {
    class WaitingTimeAlertService {
        + onWaitingOrder(OrderId, Instant) : void
        + onAssignmentCreated(OrderId, Assignment) : void
    }
}

DispatchService ..> DispatchQueue : manages waiting orders
DispatchService ..> NearestCourierSelector : selects a courier
DispatchService ..> Order : validates and assigns
DispatchService ..> Assignment : creates and persists
DispatchService ..> Courier : filters and releases
DispatchService --> DispatchExtension : publishes lifecycle events
DispatchExtension <|.. WaitingTimeAlertService : implements

note right of DispatchService
  Extract Method separated validation,
  courier selection, assignment creation, courier lookup,
  and cancelled-courier release.
  selectCourier(...) and assignCourier(...)
  keep DispatchService's dispatch flow open
  for focused future dispatch behavior.
end note

note bottom of WaitingTimeAlertService
  NTF module plugs into DispatchExtension.
  onWaitingOrder() receives queue event
  and evaluates waiting-time alerts.
  onAssignmentCreated() allows assignment
  state changes to cancel or update an alert.
end note

@enduml